Let $ABCDEF$ be a regular hexagon of side length $1$, and let $G$ be the midpoint of segment $AB$. A point $H$ is chosen inside the hexagon so that triangle $CGH$ is equilateral. Find the area of triangle $EFH$.

[asy]
import geometry;
settings.tex="none";
defaultpen(black+linewidth(0.65));
size(270);
pair[] V;for(int k=0;k<6;++k)V.push(dir(120+60*k));
pair A=V[0],B=V[1],C=V[2],D=V[3],E=V[4],F=V[5],G=(A+B)/2,H=G+rotate(60)*(C-G);
draw(A--B--C--D--E--F--cycle);draw(C--G--H--cycle);
label("A",A,(-1,1));label("B",B,(-1,0));label("C",C,(-1,-1));label("D",D,(1,-1));label("E",E,(1,0));label("F",F,(1,1));label("G",G,(-1,1));label("H",H,(1,0));
[/asy]

Three squares lie in a plane as in the figure, each sharing two of its four vertices with the other squares. The line extending a diagonal of the smallest square passes through the bottom-left vertex of the largest square. If the side lengths of the smallest and largest squares are $1$ and $3$, respectively, find the area of the shaded region.

[asy]
import geometry;
settings.tex="none";
defaultpen(black+linewidth(0.65));
size(310);
real co=(sqrt(17)+1)/6,si=(sqrt(17)-1)/6;
pair O=(0,0),A=(0,3),B=(3,0),T=A+(co,si),V=A+(si,-co),U=T+V-A;
pair mid=(U+B)/2,W=mid-rotate(90)*((B-U)/2),R=mid+rotate(90)*((B-U)/2);
path shade=V--U--W--cycle;fill(shade,gray(0.85));
for(real y=-4;y<5;y+=0.1){picture p;draw(p,(-1,y)--(5,y-3),linewidth(0.4));clip(p,shade);add(p);}
draw(O--(3,0)--(3,3)--A--cycle);draw(A--T--U--V--cycle);draw(U--R--B--W--cycle);
draw(O--T,dashed);draw(V--W);
[/asy]

An $8\times8$ grid is colored white and black as in the figure. Four black pieces and four white pieces are placed in cells of the grid. How many placements satisfy the following condition?

Every row and every column contains exactly one piece. Each black piece is in a black cell, and each white piece is in a white cell.

Pieces of the same color are indistinguishable. Placements that can be obtained from one another by rotation or reflection are counted as different.

[asy]
import geometry;
settings.tex="none";
defaultpen(black+linewidth(0.65));
size(285);
for(int i=0;i<8;++i)for(int j=0;j<8;++j){path cell=(i,j)--(i+1,j)--(i+1,j+1)--(i,j+1)--cycle;fill(cell,(i+j)%2==1?black:white);}
draw((0,0)--(8,0)--(8,8)--(0,8)--cycle);
[/asy]
